#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3640" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $h(x)$ | $z(x)$ | $h'(x)$ | $z'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right)$ at $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right) = \\dfrac{h'(x)z(x)-h(x)z'(x)}{(z(x))^2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{h(x)}{z(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(-1)z(-1)-h(-1){z}^{′}(-1)}{(z(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot 3}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "787e9681-8009-5ba8-acda-6d8830397d18" :question/math-academy-id "e-3641" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ we have\n\n$$\nf(1)=2, \\quad f'(1)=2, \\quad g(1)=-1, \\quad g'(1)=3.\n$$\n\nIf  $h(x) = \\left( f(x)-1 \\right)\\left(2g(x)+1\\right),$  compute  $h'(1).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big(uv\\Big) = u \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} +v \\dfrac{\\textrm du}{\\textrm d x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)-1$ and $v=2g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = f'(x) \\qquad  \\text{and}\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = 2g'(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(f(x)-1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)+(2g(x)+1)\\cdot {f}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2{g}^{′}(x)(f(x)-1)+{f}^{′}(x)(2g(x)+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(1) & =2{g}^{′}(1)(f(1)-1)+{f}^{′}(1)(2g(1)+1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot (2-1)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot (-1)+1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100749 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "a87386d5-4a1b-539c-aeb9-dd60181baa4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6154" :question/problem "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big( p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(p(x)+5q(x))|}_{x=-3} & ={p}^{′}(-3)+5{q}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =0+5\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100750 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "d1d0a3ec-2a84-580a-968e-53b773510853" :question/math-academy-id "e-6155" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & =f(0){g}^{′}(0)+{f}^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fdf7b57-fa6c-5c2c-be3a-d2a8d9526afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239021} {:answer/id #uuid "9d21044d-5bc1-535e-bb91-61e14957e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239421} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a2dc1c-daa1-5a37-893e-e516b10c06f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239525} {:answer/id #uuid "c67ec0cd-471c-5a08-80b1-1299eda3cb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239800} {:answer/id #uuid "d385678e-bb07-5f09-8884-65e846069242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c67ec0cd-471c-5a08-80b1-1299eda3cb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239800} :answer-field/id #uuid "e18c78c0-b7e7-5b9d-8cc8-86ab276eb94a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4b0b50f-90d4-5470-b683-6843a3c78aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-104446" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $2\\pi $ | $-3$ | $\\pi $ | $5$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4} & =f(4){g}^{′}(4)+g(4){f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =7\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "392b0b79-8325-51e9-80af-b0e2db96f3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312438} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aba0483-9c05-5996-9c78-df0105e89050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f44134b3-2bb1-57f7-a413-41c3c3c73af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341011" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(4)-(\\frac{1}{2})(2)}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-1}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb50bd7f-39cc-56cb-aa5b-7218d902f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0182abb-5f03-5f80-a3dd-0dc6384897c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65226573-de55-55b8-bdde-6256c33bf52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341013" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,g(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,{g}^{′}(4)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(4)g(4)-f(4){g}^{′}(4)}{(g(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot (-1)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9609c64-280e-5482-85de-78b23dc97263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9609c64-280e-5482-85de-78b23dc97263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313303} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7c28d9e-302c-502a-a484-226f3565f8f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e086649-7f81-509b-a9b7-a1934dc46bb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-341029" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $5$ | $0$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=1.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=1} & =3{q}^{′}(1)+4{r}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-4)+4(1) \\\\  & =-12+4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "423fd3ba-62f9-5138-b68c-a795850f01c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "423fd3ba-62f9-5138-b68c-a795850f01c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312501} :answer-field/id #uuid "007dec11-1185-591f-a7c5-e687595c6718" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89e6c8b8-1578-5971-8542-35407df630cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-341042" :question/problem "For the functions $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nu(4)=1,\\,{u}^{′}(4)=6,\\,v(4)=-2,\\,{v}^{′}(4)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))=\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{′}(x)+3{v}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}u(x)+3v(x))|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{′}(4)+3{v}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6)+3(2) \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e573fe4-0587-5479-907c-01fa86ce6686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e573fe4-0587-5479-907c-01fa86ce6686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313111} :answer-field/id #uuid "633601e8-83f3-580c-8f39-08de955b1d4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbce6b68-bc7d-5561-affe-33130a0cdf09" :question/math-academy-id "q-341450" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=(-2f(x)-3)(g(x)+1),$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$\n\n${h}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Explanation:\n\nThe product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-2f(x)-3$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =-2{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+1)+(-2f(x)-3){g}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =-2{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+1)+(-2f(2)-3){g}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =-2(2)(-3+1)+(-2(4)-3)(5) \\\\  & =-4(-2)+(-8-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =8+(-11)(5) \\\\  & =8-55 \\\\  & =-47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03aa0b84-85ab-5f27-a40c-80b94786cbb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099796} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd1ffdd-8ef7-54af-a5a3-a494a20af611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099797} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4b66f8-3ffd-5ac2-bad4-e18f7d723243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099798} {:answer/id #uuid "45cd8abe-c10e-50e1-b2f1-62e33ec96cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099799} {:answer/id #uuid "4d384832-c6be-56a0-af82-54c48acc0684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099800}] :answer-field/id #uuid "95e75162-b70a-5182-8298-a682c99e8d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099795}] :question/id #uuid "5a397261-a4b2-5058-97a1-abc48740672b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48721" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$f(1) = 2, f^{′}(1) =-3, g(1) = 4, g^{′}(1) = 2$\n\nCompute $\\frac{d}{dx}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x = 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c9c5af-ae60-5c19-98de-2006a010f6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326974} {:answer/id #uuid "725259ac-e334-586e-b4bf-e101625ee9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327923} {:answer/id #uuid "b72f49d7-33bf-5349-9709-3d90489d4014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328527} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a0ce48-bfd5-5bc5-a291-7a5731068d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328553} {:answer/id #uuid "e911496f-9a62-5fc4-92e0-55083c62392c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03c9c5af-ae60-5c19-98de-2006a010f6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326974} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc3899ec-04b9-5456-8803-fb530c320aa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "963ec6dc-aa96-5129-a681-815db2627be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-48960" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=3$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=3} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(3)g(3)-f(3){g}^{′}(3)}{(g(3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdc519dd-4fac-543e-8d13-14963e6d68ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099862} {:answer/id #uuid "d8fb0236-fc6f-5353-bdf5-7b2bf6224a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099863} {:answer/id #uuid "2eba90b3-bc95-5ecb-b006-577bd9a2a38f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099864} {:answer/id #uuid "64a78ffe-72eb-547c-99d3-ee41d2d2c856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099865} {:answer/id #uuid "7312b83b-be06-5c16-a947-186efbd67be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099866}] :answer-field/id #uuid "34fbd9d5-3505-5ad3-8b06-5872061c7a4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099861}] :question/id #uuid "26b74128-f8ea-5997-9e34-9d545612e473" :question/math-academy-id "q-4957" :question/problem "For the functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$, you're given the following data:\n$h(5) = 5, h^{′}(5) =-3, z(5) =-6, z^{′}(5) = 8$\n\nIf $w(x) = (h(x) + z(x))(3h(x) - 10)$, compute $w^{′}(5)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e56f1333-a4d0-58d4-96f3-5e95a26d5ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100354} {:answer/id #uuid "fcbc2c42-cb64-53ea-95e0-cd7d0860a2f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100355} {:answer/id #uuid "1bf343bd-3689-500e-bd04-3de821ed67ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100356} {:answer/id #uuid "6099050b-578b-5662-8940-177b865095db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100357} {:answer/id #uuid "617e9c39-3e5f-5fc7-9eea-a9311d120241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100358}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0af41a32-49c8-5dd3-953b-699af05ebe7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100353}] :question/id #uuid "ad17e802-deae-5ae1-af60-c491a8adf700" :question/math-academy-id "q-72964" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x = 2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f^{′}(x)$ | $g^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $2$ | $3$ | $1$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n\nIf $h(x) = (f(x) + 1)/(2g(x))$, compute $h^{′}(2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158ef797-3c95-5bcd-9718-13a56de44516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339318} {:answer/id #uuid "367510c1-9a7d-5efc-9a23-2d2dab4e5e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339615} {:answer/id #uuid "4bce8f0b-d42b-5d9d-86f7-87536d507436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339810} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e6fda6-a5b1-52d7-9e11-0a56fd7ca0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9b66b0-f49d-525c-93bf-5c48acfa8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340523} :answer-field/id #uuid "02a49899-89cd-5419-a9ac-3c21bb420e9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bd63bec-2f2e-5dc7-9fc2-4882af93d878" :question/math-academy-id "q-72996" :question/problem "For the functions $e(x)$ and $n(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\ne(-5)=5,\\,{e}^{′}(-5)=-6,\\,n(-5)=-7,\\,{n}^{′}(-5)=9\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))$ at $x=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))=3{e}^{′}(x)+{n}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3e(x)+n(x))|}_{x=-5} & =3{e}^{′}(-5)+{n}^{′}(-5) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-6)+9 \\\\  & =-18+9 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
